# Optional. Leave unset in the normal setup: RoadMind serves the website itself, and `npm run dev` proxies /api to
# http://127.0.0.1:8000 (see vite.config.js), so the front end just calls "/api/...".
#
# Only if the API runs somewhere else, copy this file to ".env.local" and set it (no trailing slash). The backend must
# then allow this page's origin: set ROADMIND_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173 in the project's .env.
#
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Google Maps (browser key) - OPTIONAL. The map's real road network comes from Google Maps when a key is available; without
# one it falls back to OpenStreetMap tiles (the map still works, but there is no Google live traffic).
# Create a "Maps JavaScript API" key in Google Cloud, enable the Maps JavaScript API and billing, and RESTRICT the key by
# HTTP referrer to your site (for example http://localhost:5173/* and your production address). It is a browser key, so
# it is visible to anyone who opens the site - the referrer restriction is what protects it. Never commit a real key.
# Optional because the backend can also hand the key out at runtime (GET /api/map/config); a value here wins over that.
#
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
